# Contents are listed newest arrival first, as PennMUSH keeps them: moveto() takes the object out of
# its old container's list and pushes it onto the head of the new one's (src/move.c). An imported world
# keeps the order of PennMUSH's lists; the import case leaves out SharpMUSH's own Package Manager player,
# which PennMUSH does not have.

::case contents.import  an imported room lists its contents in PennMUSH's order
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
::as wiz
think remove(iter(lcon(#0,player),name(##),,|),Package Manager,|)

::case contents.arrival  the newest arrival comes first, and arriving again makes it the newest
@create First
@create Second
@create Third
think iter(lcon(me),name(##))
drop First
get First
think iter(lcon(me),name(##))
